[{"answer":"One of the most famous cases of extinction is that of a bird known as the dodo.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/1.mp3"},{"answer":"In fact there's even a saying in English, 'as dead as the dodo',","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/2.mp3"},{"answer":"used to refer to something which no longer exists.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/3.mp3"},{"answer":"But for many centuries the dodo was alive and well,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/4.mp3"},{"answer":"although it could only be found in one place,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/5.mp3"},{"answer":"the island of Mauritius in the Indian Ocean.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/6.mp3"},{"answer":"It was a very large bird, about one metre tall,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/7.mp3"},{"answer":"and over the centuries it had lost the ability to fly,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/8.mp3"},{"answer":"but it survived happily under the trees that covered the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/9.mp3"},{"answer":"Then in the year 1507,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/10.mp3"},{"answer":"the first Portuguese ships stopped at the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/11.mp3"},{"answer":"The sailors were carrying spices back to Europe,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/12.mp3"},{"answer":"and found the island a convenient stopping place","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/13.mp3"},{"answer":"where they could stock up with food and water for the rest of the voyage,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/14-2023-07-29-12-11-07.mp3"},{"answer":"but they didn't settle on Mauritius.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/15.mp3"},{"answer":"However, in 1638","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/16.mp3"},{"answer":"the Dutch arrived and set up a colony there.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/17.mp3"},{"answer":"These first human inhabitants of the island","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/18.mp3"},{"answer":"found the dodo birds a convenient source of meat,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/19.mp3"},{"answer":"although not everyone liked the taste.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/20.mp3"},{"answer":"It's hard to get an accurate description of what the dodo actually looked like.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/21.mp3"},{"answer":"We do have some written records from sailors,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/22.mp3"},{"answer":"and a few pictures,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/23.mp3"},{"answer":"but we don't know how reliable these are.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/24.mp3"},{"answer":"The best-known picture is a Dutch painting,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/25.mp3"},{"answer":"in which the bird appears to be extremely fat,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/26.mp3"},{"answer":"but this may not be accurate -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/27.mp3"},{"answer":"an Indian painting done at the same time shows a much thinner bird.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/28.mp3"},{"answer":"Although attempts were made to preserve the bodies of some of the birds,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/29.mp3"},{"answer":"no complete specimen survives.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/30.mp3"},{"answer":"In the early 17th century","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/31.mp3"},{"answer":"four dried parts of a bird were known to exist -","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/32.mp3"},{"answer":"of these, three have disappeared,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/33.mp3"},{"answer":"so only one example of soft tissue from the dodo survives,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/34.mp3"},{"answer":"a dodo head.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/35.mp3"},{"answer":"Bones have also been found,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/36.mp3"},{"answer":"but there's only one complete skeleton in existence.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/37.mp3"},{"answer":"This single dodo skeleton has recently been the subject of scientific research","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/38.mp3"},{"answer":"which suggests that many of the earlier beliefs about dodos","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/39.mp3"},{"answer":"may have been incorrect.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/40.mp3"},{"answer":"For example,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/41.mp3"},{"answer":"early accounts of the birds mention how slow and clumsy it was,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/42.mp3"},{"answer":"but scientists now believe","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/43.mp3"},{"answer":"the bird's strong knee joints would have made it capable of movement which was not slow,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/44.mp3"},{"answer":"but actually quite fast.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/45.mp3"},{"answer":"In fact, one 17th century sailor wrote that he found the birds hard to catch.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/46.mp3"},{"answer":"It's true that the dodo's small wings wouldn't have allowed it to leave the ground,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/47.mp3"},{"answer":"but the scientists suggest that these were probably employed for balance","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/48.mp3"},{"answer":"while going over uneven ground.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/49.mp3"},{"answer":"Another group of scientists carried out analysis of the dodo's skull.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/50.mp3"},{"answer":"They found that the reports of the lack of intelligence of the dodo","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/51.mp3"},{"answer":"were not borne out by their research,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/52.mp3"},{"answer":"which suggested the bird's brain was not small,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/53.mp3"},{"answer":"but average in size.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/54.mp3"},{"answer":"In fact, in relation to its body size,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/55.mp3"},{"answer":"it was similar to that of the pigeon,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/56.mp3"},{"answer":"which is known to be a highly intelligent bird.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/57.mp3"},{"answer":"The researchers also found that the structure of the bird's skull","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/58.mp3"},{"answer":"suggested that one sense which was particularly well-developed was that of smell.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/59.mp3"},{"answer":"So the dodo may also have been particularly good at locating ripe fruit","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/60.mp3"},{"answer":"and other food in the island's thick vegetation.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/61.mp3"},{"answer":"So it looks as if the dodo was better able to survive and defend itself than was originally believed.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/62.mp3"},{"answer":"Yet less than 200 years after Europeans first arrived on the island,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/63.mp3"},{"answer":"they had become extinct.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/64.mp3"},{"answer":"So what was the reason for this?","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/65.mp3"},{"answer":"For a long time, it was believed that the dodos were hunted to extinction,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/66.mp3"},{"answer":"but scientists now believe the situation was more complicated than this.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/67.mp3"},{"answer":"Another factor may have been the new species brought to the island by the sailors.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/68.mp3"},{"answer":"These included dogs, which would have been a threat to the dodos,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/69.mp3"},{"answer":"and also monkeys,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/70.mp3"},{"answer":"which ate the fruit that was the main part of the dodos' diet.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/71.mp3"},{"answer":"These were brought to the island deliberately,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/72.mp3"},{"answer":"but the ships also brought another type of creature - rats,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/73.mp3"},{"answer":"which came to land from the ships and rapidly overran the island.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/74.mp3"},{"answer":"These upset the ecology of the island,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/75.mp3"},{"answer":"not just the dodos but other species too.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/76.mp3"},{"answer":"However,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/77.mp3"},{"answer":"they were a particular danger to the dodos","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/78.mp3"},{"answer":"because they consumed their eggs,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/79.mp3"},{"answer":"and since each dodo only laid one at a time,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/80.mp3"},{"answer":"this probably had a devastating effect on populations.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/81.mp3"},{"answer":"However,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/82.mp3"},{"answer":"we now think that probably the main cause of the birds' extinction","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/83.mp3"},{"answer":"was not the introduction of non-native species,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/84.mp3"},{"answer":"but the introduction of agriculture.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/85.mp3"},{"answer":"This meant that the forest that had once covered all the island,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/86.mp3"},{"answer":"and that had provided a perfect home for the dodo,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/87.mp3"},{"answer":"was cut down so that crops such as sugar could be grown.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/88.mp3"},{"answer":"So although the dodo had survived for thousands of years,","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/89.mp3"},{"answer":"suddenly it was gone.","audio":"https://dailydictation.com/upload/ielts-listening/ielts-cambridge-16-test-4-part-4-2023-01-06-23-00-56/90.mp3"}]
